                "added": [
                    "#Look under the car’s hood or dash board. Many cars have 2 fuse boxes, but there is no universal standard for their placement. Many manufacturers choose to keep them near the car’s engine or battery. Other manufacturer’s like to hide the fuse boxes inside the car, beneath the steering wheel. Look for a gray or black box, usually with the word “Fuses” printed on it.<ref>https://www.dmv.org/how-to-guides/fuse.php</ref>[[Image:Check Fuses Step 1 Version 7.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Check your car or repair manual if you can’t find the fuse boxes. These manuals come with new cars and are brimming with time-saving information, such as the location of the fuse boxes. This is helpful if your fuse boxes seem to be hidden pretty well. Some car manufacturers put fuse boxes in tricky locations such as in the glove box, near the brake pedal, in the trunk, or under the rear seat.<ref>https://www.familyhandyman.com/automotive/car-maintenance/replacing-auto-fuses/view-all/</ref>[[Image:Check Fuses Step 2 Version 7.jpg|center]]"
                ],
                "removed": [
                    "#Look under the car’s hood or dash board. Many cars have 2 fuse boxes, but there is no universal standard for their placement. Many manufacturers choose to keep them near the car’s engine or battery. Other manufacturer’s like to hide the fuse boxes inside the car, beneath the steering wheel. Look for a gray or black box, usually with the word “Fuses” printed on it.<ref>https://www.dmv.org/how-to-guides/fuse.php</ref>[[Image:Check Fuses Step 1 Version 6.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Check your car or repair manual if you can’t find the fuse boxes. These manuals come with new cars and are brimming with time-saving information, such as the location of the fuse boxes. This is helpful if your fuse boxes seem to be hidden pretty well. Some car manufacturers put fuse boxes in tricky locations such as in the glove box, near the brake pedal, in the trunk, or under the rear seat.<ref>https://www.familyhandyman.com/automotive/car-maintenance/replacing-auto-fuses/view-all/</ref>[[Image:Check Fuses Step 2 Version 6.jpg|center]]"
